2.0.0 2026-10
  - Participants: 656 in total: 299 from v1.1, with the same participant_id, and 357 new. One v1.1
    participant was withheld because their answers were judged to carry a high risk of re-identification.
  - Recordings: 41,831 (v1.1: 23,533). 198 recordings released in v1.1 are not linked to a record in the
    REDCap project and are not included in this version. A further 78 v1.1 recordings belonged to the
    withheld participant.
  - Data source: the pediatric data were imported into the study's REDCap project, and this version is built
    from a REDCap export rather than directly from the reproschema-ui data used for v1.1.
  - Audio files are now FLAC (lossless) instead of WAV, still 16-bit PCM, 16 kHz, mono. Where resampling
    pushed a waveform past full scale, the recording is now scaled down to its original peak instead of
    being clipped.
  - Task names: in v1.1 the number in a task name such as picture-12 counted recordings in the order they
    were made. Each task name now identifies one item, for example identifying-pictures-12,
    reading-passage-3 or repeating-words-pond, and task families were renamed (for example picture ->
    identifying-pictures, sentence -> repeating-sentences). recording_id is unchanged, so v1.1 recordings can
    be matched to v2.0.0 by joining the two versions' phenotype/task/recording.tsv on recording_id.
  - Sessions: session_id is now the session number within the participant (ses-01) instead of an
    8-character identifier. Each participant folder adds sub-<participant_id>_sessions.tsv.
  - Audio sidecars: added language, speech_type and the stimulus fields (stimulus_text, stimulus_source,
    stimulus_asset); prompts is replaced by the stimulus fields.
  - phenotype/task/recording.tsv grows from 11 to 31 columns, adding the task name, language, instructions,
    stimulus, speech type, recording order and timing, and audio sample rate and channel count. The device,
    platform and browser columns are present but empty for this cohort.
  - New phenotype/enrollment folder: participant.tsv (site, whether any data were collected remotely,
    selected language), eligibility.tsv and enrollment_form.tsv.
  - Demographics: race is now one column per option. State or province and form duration were added.
  - Medical conditions: multi-select answers are now one column per option, and the number of days from each
    surgery or procedure to the participant's first session was added.
  - Phenotype JSON files now describe each table and give each column's description, question and choices.
  - New files: data_explorer.html, LICENSE and this CHANGES file. The README was rewritten.

1.1.0 2026-06
  - Released on Synapse (doi:10.7303/syn74341287.2).

1.0.0 2026-04
